# transient per-run source pulls — never committed (see ../CLAUDE.md)
raw/

# BUILD ARTIFACT, not data. offer/build_data.py regenerates it offline from the
# committed listings.csv in about a second, it is 1.4 MB, and it changes on EVERY
# scrape — committing it would add ~75 MB of churn a year to a public repo for a file
# nothing needs. Same reasoning as raw/: transient and reproducible.
#
# data.js is NOT ignored, deliberately: it is 3x smaller, changes only when the sold
# data does (rarely), and index.html white-screens without it — so a fresh clone should
# just work. The Pages workflow re-bakes it anyway, so a stale commit can't publish
# numbers that disagree with the CSVs behind them.
offer/listings.js

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# secrets backstop (this repo is PUBLIC)
.env*
*secret*
*webhook*
*.key
*.pem
